' =====================================================================
' RoboFetch - State machine: the robot duty cycle (complex feature C1)
' Health states outrank activity: an overheated robot is in COOLDOWN
' whatever the task manager believes it is doing.
' Source: robofetch_core/robot_state_node.py (_duty_state), task_manager.py
' =====================================================================
@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor White
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #FBFCFE
  BorderColor #34495E
  ArrowColor #34495E
}

title Robot Duty-Cycle State Machine

[*] --> CHARGING : boots docked at the station

CHARGING --> IDLE : battery at ready level
IDLE --> WORKING : an accepted order is dequeued
IDLE --> RETURNING : idle timeout expires
WORKING --> RETURNING : order finished (delivered or failed)
WORKING --> COOLDOWN : temperature reaches the limit
COOLDOWN --> RETURNING : temperature falls below resume level
RETURNING --> CHARGING : station reached
RETURNING --> FAULT : station unreachable
CHARGING --> IDLE : recharged
IDLE --> FAULT : condition below the maintenance floor
FAULT --> [*]

note right of COOLDOWN
  Entered from the measured
  temperature, not from a command.
  Admission control reads this state
  and refuses new work while it holds.
end note

note left of RETURNING
  Reached automatically after the idle
  timeout, so the robot parks and
  recharges instead of stopping wherever
  the last delivery left it.
end note

@enduml
